   "kind": "reply",
   "text": "The Theme collection now has a High contrast mode. The Showcase page shows the Order screen three times, side by side: the original in Light, a copy in Dark and a copy in High contrast. I saved it as `order-themes.fig` next to `order.fig`, which is unchanged. grafta read the saved file back and it matched, but I haven't opened it in Figma, so that's the remaining check.\n\n**High contrast values** (a black base with white text and a yellow accent):\n\n| Variable | High contrast |\n|---|---|\n| Background | `#000000` |\n| Surface | `#0A0A0A` |\n| Ink | `#FFFFFF` |\n| Muted | `#E0E0E0` |\n| Border | `#FFFFFF` (makes the card's outline stand out) |\n| Accent | `#FFE500` |\n| Accent soft | `#000000` |\n| On accent | `#000000` |\n| Track | `#6E6E6E` (keeps the unfilled part of the progress bar visible) |\n\n**Checks:**\n- I rendered all three screens and each looked right, with nothing missing or broken in the layout.\n- All 9 text layers on the High contrast screen pass WCAG AA contrast. Ratios run from 14.7:1 to 21:1 against a 4.5:1 minimum. The lowest is the grey secondary text on the card.\n\nThese were my own colour choices, so tell me if you want different ones, such as a light high-contrast theme instead."
